+
+### Decisions made without asking
+- One widget instead of separate carousel, wheel and stack widgets. The path, effects and presets cover them, and push/pop is the same panel with Transitions.
+- Children are real widgets (designer-droppable, any Widget Blueprint), not a virtualized data list. There is culling (Cull Distance, opacity 0 and off-screen items aren't laid out or painted), but no widget pooling.
+- `AddItem` etc. animate by default, so filling a list in Construct plays as a staggered intro. Pass `bAnimate = false`, or turn off Animate Changes, for an instant fill.
+- Item Clicked fires on any click the list sees, including on a button item (alongside its own On Clicked).
+- Select-tick sounds are rate-limited in real time by the list (`MinTimeBetweenTicks`). `FUISoundSetSettings::MinTimeBetweenPlays` counts game time, which stops in a paused menu.
+- Palette category "NameTBD", as for Shape Box.
+
+### Reviewed before delivery
+An independent pass over the new files found no definite compile errors. It did find these logic bugs, now fixed:
+- Popping the focused front item didn't move the selection or gamepad focus to the item that slid in, because the index stayed 0. `SetSelected` now has a `bForce` parameter.
+- Re-adding a leaving item froze it.
+- A looping list's position was re-wrapped mid-press, which gave the wrong fling target.
+- Starting a drag released every user's mouse capture. It now releases only the pressing user's.
+- `InsertChild` could return a slot that was already leaving.
+- A stale touch press blocked focus-driven scrolling.
+- A click reported a stale index after the items changed mid-press.
+- Leaving items outlived their UObjects on release.
+- At the end of the list, the wheel swallowed fractional trackpad deltas, and gamepad navigation leaving the list played the edge sound.
+- Tint's Custom easing had no curve.
+- The designer path-guide loop used a float step.
 
